WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.959
So now you've saved a lot of words,
created LingQs, you've saved, I hope,

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:08.639
phrases and you're probably wondering
how you can possibly review all of these

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:14.009
words? The good news is you don't have to
review them all. In fact, if you're

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:18.810
creating a lot of LingQs, as I always do,
I can't possibly review them all. You

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:25.230
review some of them. You can review them
after each page when you're reading, you

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:31.199
can go to the vocabulary page and select
a different group of words to review, you

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:36.440
can choose which of the different
activities you want to use, you know

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:42.719
flashcards, multiple-choice, dictation,
reverse flash cards. It's more an

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:47.430
opportunity to increase your
attentiveness to the language, especially

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:52.800
if you create tags. Even creating tags
focuses your attention on these words

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.879
and phrases. But don't think you can
review them all, you can't. Review some of

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.780
them and spend most of your time
enjoyably listening and reading and

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:07.339
seeing all of your LingQs show up in
yellow and eventually they turn to white.

